# Project AI Instructions — Vendor Solution Intelligence Platform

## Tech Stack (DO NOT CHANGE)
- Framework: React 18 + TypeScript (strict mode)
- Build Tool: Vite
- Styling: Tailwind CSS only — no inline styles, no CSS modules
- Component Library: shadcn/ui (Radix UI primitives)
- Icons: Lucide React
- State: Zustand
- Tables: TanStack Table v8
- Charts: Recharts
- Package Manager: pnpm only — never npm or yarn

## Design System (ALWAYS FOLLOW)
- Colors: use CSS variables from theme.css only
- Dark theme by default (bg: #0F1117, surface: #1A1D27)
- Typography: Inter font, defined size scale in theme.css
- Spacing: Tailwind spacing scale only (no arbitrary px values)
- Border radius: rounded-lg for cards, rounded-md for inputs
- All new components must follow existing shadcn/ui patterns

## Component Rules
- Every new UI element = a new component in src/app/components/
- No component longer than 150 lines — split if larger
- Props must be TypeScript typed (no `any`)
- Use existing components before creating new ones

## What NOT To Do
- Never install MUI, Bootstrap, Chakra UI, or Ant Design
- Never use styled-components or emotion
- Never write raw CSS files
- Never use class components
- Never use Create React App patterns
- Never change vite.config.ts or tailwind.config.ts without asking

## When Adding New Features
1. Check src/app/components/ for existing reusable components first
2. Follow the dark theme color tokens in theme.css
3. Use shadcn/ui primitives (Button, Card, Dialog, Table, Badge)
4. Match the existing visual density and spacing of the dashboard
